#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119743 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119559 :question/id #uuid "98c98a56-ca57-5dc6-9dc4-c40da53806f7" :question/math-academy-id "e-3063" :question/problem "Write down the integral that gives the arc length of the curve  $\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle 3 \\sin t, \\: 2\\sin 2t \\rangle$\nfrom $t =\\dfrac {3\\pi} 2$  to $t = 2\\pi.$\n\n![](images/57/574a16e843a9c81e5fc9ddbbe2c0dc2c308ffcac4991bcbf48c7f45b4871c93b.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc0992a-423e-5023-98d5-9d53c3b77788" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048999} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050860} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051021}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545074 :question-generator/id #uuid "6117e984-c7a5-59c5-a43b-68006373fedc" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186119743.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c60eb52-e275-5f9e-8b64-8f24c6fbbbff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2\\cos^{2} 2t + 3\\sin^{2} 3t}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117772} {:answer/id #uuid "5068c443-8395-505c-92d8-71cea0dfc17e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/re